The more constrained (simpler) model fits significantly worse than the less constrained (more complex) model — the freed parameter(s) contribute meaningfully to model fit








Q2. A modification index of 24.5 suggests adding a cross-loading of anx2 onto the EFF factor. Should you add this path?





Not necessarily — only if there is a substantive theoretical justification. Adding paths purely because their MI is large constitutes post-hoc model fishing and inflates Type I error.




No — modification indices should never be consulted after model fitting




Yes — any MI above 10 must be freed to achieve acceptable model fit




Yes — a larger MI always means the path is theoretically meaningful

